{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":251822,"duration_api_ms":249660,"ttft_ms":2845,"ttft_stream_ms":1274,"time_to_request_ms":11,"num_turns":54,"result":"# Investigation Report\n\n## Task Summary\nVerify that adding `salt/cache/sqlite3_cache.py` as a new driver module — discovered and dispatched purely by Salt's existing dynamic-loading mechanism — requires no changes anywhere outside the `salt/cache` cell, and that the module contract (dunder-globals injection, `__virtualname__` resolution, no-`init_kwargs` fallback) is correctly understood before implementation.\n\n## Candidate Cells\n| Cell | Reason | Priority |\n|---|---|---|\n| `salt/cache` | Modification target — new driver concretization | High |\n| `salt/loader` | Read-only dispatch mechanism the new driver plugs into | Medium |\n\n## Tracing Summary\n- `salt.loader.cache(opts)` (`salt/loader/__init__.py:1692-1705`) builds a `LazyLoader` over `_module_dirs(opts, \"cache\", \"cache\")` with `tag=\"cache\"`. `_module_dirs` (`salt/loader/__init__.py:121-138`) walks `SALT_BASE_PATH/cache` (i.e. the `salt/cache/` directory itself) plus any `extension_modules/cache` dir — every `.py` file in `salt/cache/` is a discoverable candidate purely by filesystem presence. **No enumeration/registration list of driver names exists anywhere** — dropping in `sqlite3_cache.py` is sufficient for discovery.\n- Module naming: `LazyLoader._process_virtual` (`salt/loader/lazy.py:1342-1453`) sets the dict key used for dispatch (`module_name`) to `__virtualname__` when the module defines one and `__virtual__()` doesn't return `False` (lines 1395, 1417-1421, 1447-1453). This confirms `__virtualname__ = \"sqlite3\"` in the new module makes it addressable as `sqlite3.store`, `sqlite3.fetch`, etc. — exactly matching how `mysql_cache.py` (`__virtualname__ = \"mysql\"`, `salt/cache/mysql_cache.py:97`) and `redis_cache.py`/`etcd_cache.py`/`consul.py`/`etcd3_cache.py` (same pattern, confirmed via grep) become selectable as `cache: mysql`/`redis`/etc.\n- Dispatch from the facade: `Cache.__init__` (`salt/cache/__init__.py:62-74`) sets `self.driver = opts.get(\"cache\", salt.config.DEFAULT_MASTER_OPTS[\"cache\"])` (default `\"localfs\"`, `salt/config/__init__.py:1429` et al. — confirmed by grep, only appears as a *default value*, never as a validated choices-list/enum). `Cache.store/fetch/flush/list/contains/updated/clean_expired` (`salt/cache/__init__.py:131-366`) all build the dispatch key as `f\"{self.driver}.{funcname}\"` and call `self.modules[fun](...)` — a plain dict lookup into the `LazyLoader`, with no allowlist check. Setting `cache: sqlite3` in opts is therefore sufficient end-to-end.\n- `self.kwargs` (`salt/cache/__init__.py:80-85`) is a `cached_property` that calls `self.modules[f\"{self.driver}.init_kwargs\"](self._kwargs)` inside a `try/except KeyError`, falling back to `{}` if the driver has no `init_kwargs` function. `mysql_cache.py` and `redis_cache.py` define no `init_kwargs` at all (confirmed: grep of `__func_alias__`/`__virtualname__` region shows no `init_kwargs` in either file) and instead read `__opts__` directly inside their own `_init_client()`. This confirms the planned sqlite3 driver can safely omit `init_kwargs` and read `sqlite3.database`/`sqlite3.table_name`/`sqlite3.timeout` from `__opts__` inside its own `_init_client()`, exactly like `mysql_cache._init_client()` (`salt/cache/mysql_cache.py:227-264`) does.\n- Dunder-injection: `LazyLoader` packs `\"__context__\": context` and `\"__opts__\": opts` into every loaded module's namespace (`salt/loader/__init__.py:362,365` and repeated at every loader-construction call site, e.g. lines 488, 561, 601, 654/657, 733). `mysql_cache.py` already relies on this — e.g. `__context__.pop(\"mysql_client\", None)` (`salt/cache/mysql_cache.py:113`) and `opts = copy.deepcopy(__opts__)` (`salt/cache/mysql_cache.py:232`) — proving `__context__`/`__opts__` are live module globals by the time driver functions run. The planned `_init_client()` storing a `sqlite3.Connection` + `threading.Lock` in `__context__` is the same validated pattern.\n\n## Data Flow Analysis\n`opts[\"cache\"] = \"sqlite3\"` → `Cache.driver = \"sqlite3\"` → `Cache.modules[\"sqlite3.store\"]` resolved via `LazyLoader` file-discovery + `__virtualname__` match against `salt/cache/sqlite3_cache.py` → driver function executes against `__opts__`/`__context__` injected by the loader → data serialized via `salt.payload.dumps`/`loads` (mirroring `mysql_cache.py`/`redis_cache.py`, not the file-object-based `salt.payload.dump`/`load` used only by `localfs.py`) → persisted to the SQLite file on disk, surviving process restart because the file (not `__context__`, which is per-process) is the durable store.\n\n## Manifest Algorithm Analysis\n`salt/cache/CODEMANIFEST` currently documents `Cache::LocalFSBackend()` as the sole concretization, with the explicit statement: *\"The driver-module relationship is modeled here with the DSL's mutation notation (Cache::LocalFSBackend) because it is a real concretization-without-inheritance pattern: the driver is a plain module of same-named functions dynamically dispatched through a LazyLoader, not a Python subclass of Cache.\"* This is a general statement about the *pattern*, not an exhaustive enumeration — adding a sibling `Cache::SQLite3Backend()` concretization block (same shape: `location: sqlite3_cache.py`, `store`/`fetch`/`flush` methods documented) is additive and consistent with the documented pattern; it does not require editing the `Imports`/`Annotations` header, which already generically describes \"the driver\" as a category, not a fixed single instance (other undocumented-in-manifest drivers like `mysql_cache.py`, `redis_cache.py`, `etcd_cache.py`, `consul.py` already coexist with only `LocalFSBackend` documented — confirming the manifest documents a *representative* concretization, not a closed set).\n\n## Affected Usages\n| Usage | Cell | Classification | Reason |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| — | — | — | No `Usages` are declared in `salt/cache/CODEMANIFEST` (`usages: []`) and no project-level `.goga/config.yml` `codemanifest.usages`/`codemanifest.annotations` exist (confirmed \"Option not found\" in prior step). No usage files are affected by this change. |\n\n## Rejected Hypotheses\n- **Hypothesis: a fixed driver-name registry/choices list must be updated (e.g. in `salt/config/__init__.py` validation or a CLI arg-parser).** Rejected — grep across `salt/` for cache-backend enumerations found only *default value* assignments (`\"cache\": \"localfs\"` at 5 locations in `salt/config/__init__.py`, none of which are `choices=[...]` validators or enums) plus two unrelated `\"localfs\"` string literals (`salt/cluster/consensus/storage.py:99` comparing `driver` at runtime — not a registry; `salt/tokens/localfs.py` — an unrelated token-cache module, not the data cache). No evidence of a closed registry anywhere.\n- **Hypothesis: driver modules must define `init_kwargs` for `Cache.kwargs` to work.** Rejected with direct evidence — `Cache.kwargs` (`salt/cache/__init__.py:80-85`) explicitly catches `KeyError` and defaults to `{}`; `mysql_cache.py`/`redis_cache.py` (both without `init_kwargs`) are existing, working, shipped drivers.\n- **Hypothesis: `__context__`/`__opts__` might not be available inside a cache driver module at call time.** Rejected — `LazyLoader` packs both into every loaded module's globals at multiple construction sites, and `mysql_cache.py` already depends on this exact injection in production code.\n\n## Confirmed Root Cause\nNot applicable in the traditional bug sense — this is an additive feature. Root confirmation: the cache-driver extension point is genuinely open (filesystem-discovery + `__virtualname__`-based dispatch, no closed registry), so a new `salt/cache/sqlite3_cache.py` module implementing the standard driver function set is sufficient, with zero required edits to `salt/cache/__init__.py`, `salt/loader/__init__.py`, or `salt/config/__init__.py`. The `\"cache\": \"localfs\"` default value in `salt/config/__init__.py` remains untouched, preserving default behavior for all non-opted-in deployments.\n\n## Confidence Level\n**HIGH** — every claim above is backed by direct file:line evidence from the actual implementation (`salt/loader/__init__.py`, `salt/loader/lazy.py`, `salt/cache/__init__.py`, `salt/cache/mysql_cache.py`, `salt/config/__init__.py`) and corroborated by an existing, shipped, structurally-identical driver (`mysql_cache.py`) that already proves the no-`init_kwargs` / `__context__`-persistent-connection / `__virtualname__`-dispatch pattern works end-to-end. Test infrastructure (`tests/pytests/functional/cache/test_localfs.py`, `test_mysql.py`, `tests/pytests/unit/cache/test_mysql_cache.py`) confirms no shared `conftest.py` fixture is required beyond the global `minion_opts` fixture already used by every existing backend test — new tests can follow that exact pattern with no additional wiring.\n\n## Breaking Change Assessment\n1. **Will existing function call with same arguments produce different behavior?** NO — no existing function in `salt/cache/__init__.py`, `salt/loader/__init__.py`, or any existing driver module is modified. Only a new file is added.\n2. **Will existing file paths change?** NO — no files are moved, renamed, or removed.\n3. **Will output format change?** NO — the new driver is only reachable when an operator explicitly sets `cache: sqlite3`; the default (`localfs`) and all other existing drivers produce identical output as before.\n4. **Will return value semantics change?** NO — same reasoning; `Cache` facade semantics for existing drivers are untouched.\n5. **Will manifest-defined guarantees be altered?** NO — the existing `Cache::LocalFSBackend()` manifest entry and the header `Imports`/`Annotations` are left intact; only a new sibling concretization entry is added.\n6. **Will existing tests break?** NO — no existing test file is modified; new test files are additive (`test_sqlite3_cache.py`, `test_sqlite3.py`).\n\n**No breaking change detected.** Pipeline may proceed to Planning.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"c481760d-dfdf-4d43-98c7-7978d7d3a9ff","total_cost_usd":1.9085510999999997,"usage":{"input_tokens":56,"cache_creation_input_tokens":125994,"cache_read_input_tokens":2518947,"output_tokens":26449,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":125994,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":56,"outputTokens":26449,"cacheReadInputTokens":2518947,"cacheCreationInputTokens":125994,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.9085510999999997,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"d0768c61-c94d-4688-8ccd-95c241024474"}
